SUMMARY:Corn Hole Tournament at AMB
DESCRIPTION:Asheville Social Club\n**Hey y’all!! We’re gonna host a Co
 rn Hole Tournament at Appalachian Mountain Brewery!**\n**We’re gonna hos
 t a double elimination tournament!** **AMB has four cornhole board sets\, 
 and several of us have more. We’re going to run eight games at a time if
  needed.** **Come out and let’s have some fun\,** **and support a great 
 local business!**\n\n**Grab your partner and come out and play! If you do 
 not have a partner\, you can** **partner with someone at the event.** **Do
  not let not having a partner stop you from coming out for this event.**\n
 \n**Be there at 5:00 to register teams of two\, or to find a partner at th
 e event. Registration closes at 5:45. First games start at 6:00.**\n\n**We
  are going to have two brackets.**\n\n**Competition**\n\n**Fun**\n\n* **Co
 mpetition bracket will be a paid bracket that will have a $5 entry fee per
  team of two. There will be prizes for 1st\, 2nd and 3rd place winners.**\
 n\n* **Fun bracket will be for teams or individuals that want to participa
 te\, but not be in the running for prizes.**\n\n**Brackets close when we r
 each 12 teams in each.**\n**So sign up and get your team’s spot!**\n\n**
 When you sign up for the event\, please post a comment stating whether you
  want to do competition or fun bracket. The $10 will be accepted the day o
 f the event.**\n\n**https://www.amb.beer/mills-river**\n\n**This is gonna 
 be fun!!**\n\n**The object of cornhole is to reach exactly 21 points first
 . Teams score points by tossing bags onto the board (1 point) or through t
 he hole (3 points). Play alternates until all 8 bags are tossed\, and scor
 es cancel each other out at the end of each round (cancellation scoring).S
 etup &**\n\n**GameplayDistance: Place boards 27 feet apart (measured from 
 the front edge to the front edge). For a casual backyard game\, you can ad
 just this distance based on player ability.**\n\n**Teams: Played with 2 pl
 ayers (Singles) or 4 players (Doubles). In doubles\, teammates stand direc
 tly across from each other at opposite boards.**\n\n**Turns: Players throw
  underhand and must stay behind the foul line (the front edge of the board
 ). Players alternate turns throwing one bag at a time until all 8 bags hav
 e been tossed.**\n\n**Scoring: in the hole: 3 points. On the board: 1 poin
 t. Foul bag: 0 points (e.g.\, if a bag hits the ground first or if a playe
 r steps on or crosses the foul line).Points are calculated using cancellat
 ion scoring.**\n\n**The team with the higher score in the round subtracts 
 the lower team's score to get the net points for that round. For example\,
  if Team A scores 5 points and Team B scores 3 points\, Team A is awarded 
 2 points for that frame.**
